WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.269
- Just before the new
year, British socialite

00:00:01.269 --> 00:00:04.000
and Jeffrey Epstein par
amour, Ghislaine Maxwell

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.250
was convicted of sex
trafficking of a minor,

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.570
transporting a minor
with the intent to engage

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.040
in criminal sexual activity,

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.170
conspiracy to entice a minor to travel

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.570
for the purpose of engaging
in illegal sex acts,

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.200
and conspiracy to transport
a minor with the intent

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.720
to engage in criminal sexual activity.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.782
The Maxwell trial was a bonanza
for conspiracy theorists

00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:24.280
because the characters include

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.550
some of the most famous
people in the world.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.170
A victim said that she
was recruited by Epstein

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.870
when she worked as a 15-year-old

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.450
at Donald Trump's Florida
resort, Mar-a-Lago.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.740
One of the prosecutors was Maurene Comey,

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.430
daughter of James Comey.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.670
Super lawyer, Alan
Dershowitz helped Epstein

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.900
to get a plea deal for
abusing young girls,

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.600
and then was accused of
participating in the sexual abuse

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.930
of two girls in Epstein's orbit.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.190
Friend of Jeffrey, Prince
Andrew partied with Epstein

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:51.400
at Mar-a-Lago and is in
the midst of a legal battle

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.990
with a woman who says Andrew
and Epstein abused her.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:55.330
Bill Clinton admitted to flying

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.210
with Jeffrey Epstein four times.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.730
Donald Trump, that he
fell out with Epstein,

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.450
but complemented Maxwell,
saying, "I wish her well."

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.120
- I just wish her well, frankly.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.640
- And of course, Epstein
and Maxwell are known

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.260
to be in the orbit of many
famous Democrats and Republicans.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.890
And then of course,
there's Epstein himself

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.210
who killed himself in prison

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.520
before he could be tried in court,

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.210
launching speculation that he was murdered

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.050
at the behest of the Clintons,
or by then President Trump,

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:21.070
or by the CIA, or some
other shadowy cabal.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:23.460
But all of these famous
names and outlandish theories

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.030
tend to diminish what the victims say

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.130
actually happened to them,

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.450
that they were sexually abused by Epstein

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.690
and aided and abetted by
Maxwell when they were minors.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.840
So in this video, will
explain what really happened

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:34.860
in the Maxwell trial.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.360
What did the victims say
about Epstein and Maxwell?

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.110
How many years could she face in prison

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.400
and what happens next?

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.150
And most importantly, why could one juror

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.318
undo the entire trial?

00:01:45.318 --> 00:01:48.235
(triumphant music)

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.370
So let's start at the beginning.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.170
Who is Ghislaine Maxwell?

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.900
Maxwell is a French-born,
Oxford-educated socialite.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.550
She's the daughter of Robert Maxwell

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.110
who escaped Nazi persecution,

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.520
in what was then Czechoslovakia,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.910
on the eve of World War II.

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.170
Robert immigrated to France
and then to Great Britain

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:04.930
where he eventually became
a member of parliament

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:05.830
for six years.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.630
Ghislaine is the youngest
of nine children.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.000
In 1991, her father drowned on a yacht

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.760
named the Lady Ghislaine
after his beloved daughter.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.593
By the end of his life,

00:02:13.593 --> 00:02:16.020
Robert was media tycoon who
owned several newspapers

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.530
and publishing companies.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.320
After his death, the
world learned that Robert

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.950
had been laundering pension
funds and embezzling money.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.080
But despite the scandal,

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.740
Ghislaine Maxwell's family connections

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.030
enabled her to form relationships

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.810
with rich and famous people
from around the world,

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.320
which she leveraged once she
met Epstein in the early 1990s.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.130
Epstein was an incredibly wealthy man.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.730
Though it seems that
nobody knows precisely

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.020
how he made his money or how much he made.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.720
Epstein was briefly a professor,

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.930
hired by the father of Former
Attorney General William Barr.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.836
Later, he became a
trader for Bear Stearns,

00:02:43.836 --> 00:02:46.460
where he was made partner
in just four years.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.620
After leaving Stearns,

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.400
Epstein went into business for himself.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.080
Most of Epstein's acquaintances
have said that Epstein

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.150
was a money manager who
only accepted clients

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.530
who had $1 billion or more.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.480
Epstein eventually
purchased a private island,

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.250
and had two jets, which he
used to entertain friends.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.640
He also became a philanthropist,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.620
allegedly giving away hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.630
to charitable causes.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.230
But in reality, it seems
that the Epstein Foundation

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.730
turned out to be a mirage
to gain tax exemptions

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.380
and rehabilitate his image

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.300
after his 2005 Florida sex abuse case.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.340
In 2005, the police
investigated the financier

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.200
for abusing underage girls.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.970
One of the accusers
told the "Miami Herald"

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.220
that he was preying on 14-year-old girls

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.410
who were, quote, "basically homeless".

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:28.490
At the time, Epstein
called on Alan Dershowitz,

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:29.830
who attacked the accuser's character

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.970
and negotiated a non-prosecution agreement

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:34.240
that allowed Epstein to
plead guilty to one count

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.720
of solicitation with
no additional charges.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.960
He served 13 months in a
county jail on work release.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.440
As longtime Legal Eagles know,

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.900
the prosecutor who negotiated
the deal was Alex Acosta,

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.350
who later became the secretary
of labor for Donald Trump.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.500
And Acosta resigned after
criticism of the deal.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.450
You can watch my video
about Epstein and Acosta

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.570
for more information.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:54.640
It is, to put it mildly, bonkers.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:57.210
Now some have suggested
that Epstein also made money

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:59.230
by blackmailing his
rich and famous friends.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.890
When the FBI raided his properties,

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.690
they found hundreds and perhaps thousands

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.410
of sexually suggestive
photographs of nude females.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.390
The FBI also seized compact discs

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:11.090
that were labeled with the
words, "Young blank name + name".

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:12.960
Virginia Roberts Giuffre
publicly accused Epstein

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.450
and Britain's Prince
Andrew of sexual abuse.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.640
She says American law
enforcement have video footage

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.270
of her having sex with members

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.480
of Epstein's elite friend group.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.940
Now all of this indicates that authorities

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.180
have significant information
about Epstein's activities,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.180
and they know that he broke the law.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.580
But in 2019, Epstein
committed suicide in jail.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.820
But despite years of
accusations that Maxwell

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.330
participated in the abuse,

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.470
she managed to stay on the lam for years

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:39.450
until she was arrested at
home in New Hampshire in 2021.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.417
Federal prosecutor, Alison
Moe called her quote,

00:04:41.417 --> 00:04:42.650
"A sophisticated predator

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:45.480
and the key to Epstein's
criminal abuse of girls."

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.180
Which takes us to the
trial of Ghislaine Maxwell.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.720
Maxwell stood trial on six charges

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.720
of committing sex crimes against minors.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:56.280
The crimes happened between 1994 and 2004.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.030
Then we do know that Epstein had a history

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:00.340
of abusing under-aged girls,
often during encounters

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:02.620
that started with a girl
giving Epstein a massage.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.510
Epstein promised girls to help
with their personal problems,

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.040
pledged to fund their educations,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.680
and made them believe that
he would help them launch

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.820
their careers in music,
massage, or any area

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.190
where the girl expressed interest.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.500
The Epstein encounters
happened at his properties

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.370
all over the world.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.210
Four victims testified during this trial,

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.320
helping prosecutors to
show a pattern of abuse.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.220
So what was Maxwell's
alleged role in this?

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.410
Well, federal prosecutor said

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.600
that she actively groomed under-aged girls

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.200
and then brought them
into Epstein's household.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.270
The victims testified
that Maxwell facilitated

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:30.780
the abuse of under-aged girls.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.250
She gained their trust
by taking them shopping,

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.540
inviting them to luxurious
estates, and on expensive trips,

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.670
all the while, making it
seem like they were safe.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.650
But then she basically acted
like a madam and an accomplice,

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.917
luring the girls into sexual
encounters with Epstein

00:05:43.917 --> 00:05:45.270
and Maxwell herself.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:46.950
The prosecution showed
that during this timeframe,

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.580
Epstein transferred over
$30 million to Maxwell.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:52.050
So how did Epstein and
Maxwell coerce girls

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.050
into traveling with them?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:54.790
Well, witnesses said that they pretended

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.420
that they were mentoring the girls.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.380
One witness testified
that Epstein paid for her

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.260
to attend a performing arts camp.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.350
Another witnesses said that
Epstein funded her travels

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:03.506
under the guise of helping her improve

00:06:03.506 --> 00:06:04.970
her college prospects.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.490
Prosecutors told the
jury that the evidence

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.870
would prove that all of these activities

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:10.770
were just subtext for grooming
the girls for sexual abuse.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.970
The prosecution's expert
witness, Lisa Rokio,

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.310
who was a therapist,

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.900
claimed that the predator
selected vulnerable victims,

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.610
isolate them from friends and family,

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.020
earn their trust with money and gifts.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.750
And then begin the abuse. One
of the victims said that she

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.150
was in a vulnerable position
when she met Epstein.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.130
Her father had died,

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:28.540
and Epstein promised to
fund her college education.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.040
The woman who testified said that Maxwell

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:32.550
first presented herself
as a wise, older sister,

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.020
but then started casually mentioning

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:36.360
how they should touch
Epstein during a massage.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.650
Their accounts of the abuse
were supported by people

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:39.770
were worked for Epstein.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.430
Juan Alessi, a former
housekeeper in Palm Beach,

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:44.100
said he was asked to drive Maxwell

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.740
around to the massage parlors
and spas in the local area,

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.640
looking for girls that they could recruit.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.080
David Rodgers flew
Epstein for over 30 years.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.210
He kept a meticulous personal flight log

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:54.620
of the more than 1,000 times

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.540
he flew one of Epstein's private planes.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.350
A redacted version of the flight logs

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.860
was entered into evidence.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.680
And these heavily redacted
flight logs were pretty damning.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:05.100
The logs showed that Epstein
and other passengers flew

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.020
with some of the victims
from 1996 to 1998,

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:10.240
confirming one of the victim's stories.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.630
The flight logs also confirmed
that Epstein's accuser,

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.180
Virginia Giuffre had indeed flown

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.980
on the airplane with Epstein.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.710
Giuffre has accused Prince Andrew

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:21.010
of sexually abusing her
when she was 17 years old.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:22.210
Prince Andrew, for his part,

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.710
admits hanging out with Epstein,
but denies the allegations.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.810
Lawrence Wysocki, one of Epstein's pilots

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:29.020
said he never witnessed
sexual activity on the planes.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:30.560
However, he also said
that the cockpit door

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:33.090
was always kept closed
during flights on the plane

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.070
nicknamed the "Lolita Express".

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:37.170
Now the most serious
charge against Maxwell

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.990
was for sex trafficking a minor.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:41.047
The indictment said that Maxwell, quote,

00:07:41.047 --> 00:07:42.850
"Assisted, facilitated, and contributed

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.970
to Jeffrey Epstein's
abuse of minor girls by,

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:47.910
among other things, helping
Epstein to recruit, groom,

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.880
and ultimately abuse victims
known to Maxwell and Epstein

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.460
to be under the age of 18.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:55.727
Now, sex trafficking is
covered by 18 U.S.C. 1591.

00:07:55.727 --> 00:07:59.020
And it applies to anyone who
knowingly recruits, entices,

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.290
harbors, transports, provides, or obtains,

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.750
by any means a person,
knowing that the person

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.620
has not attained the age of 18 years

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:09.110
and will be caused to engage
in a commercial sex act.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.350
Now, this charge relates
solely to Maxwell's actions

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:12.800
towards victim Caroline,

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.670
who was abused by Epstein
when she was in her teens.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:17.450
Caroline, who withheld her last name,

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.050
told the jury that when she was 14,

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:21.520
she was sexually abused
by a Maxwell and Epstein.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.630
She testified about setting
up a massage room for Epstein,

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:27.640
when Maxwell came into the room
and touched Caroline's body.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.140
Caroline estimates that she
visited Epstein's Florida house

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:33.550
over 100 times between 2001 and 2004.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:36.890
And each time she visited,
$300 in cash was left for her

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.300
on the bathroom sink.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.540
For sex trafficking a minor,
Maxwell faces up to 40 years

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:43.740
of imprisonment as a first-time offender.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.830
The jury also found
Maxwell guilty of enticing

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:46.810
a minor to travel

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.390
and transporting a minor
across state lines.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.810
Federal criminal law
prohibits a wide range

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.960
of activities relating
to transporting people

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.110
and traveling across state
lines or internationally

00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:59.480
for the purpose of engaging
in illegal sexual conduct.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:02.962
18 U.S.C. 2422 prohibits anyone
from knowingly persuading,

00:09:02.962 --> 00:09:06.220
inducing, enticing, or coercing
an individual to travel

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.920
in interstate or foreign commerce

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:09.660
with the purpose of
engaging in prostitution

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:12.570
or any criminal activity
or attempting to do so.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.970
Victim Jane who testified
under an assumed name,

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.070
said that when she was 14 years old,

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.600
Maxwell and Epstein approached her

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.340
at an arts camp in Michigan.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:22.360
This was the beginning of
several years of abuse,

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:25.150
which happened at Epstein's
Palm Beach mansion.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:27.040
Jane testified that she was forced

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.910
to give Epstein a massage,
that he turned sexual.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.530
And she testified that
Maxwell was often in the room

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.030
during that abuse.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.860
Jane said that Maxwell gained her trust,

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:37.640
and made her feel like
she was an older sister,

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.850
which paved the way for the abuse.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:44.050
The abuse occurred when Jane
was 14, 15, and 16 years old.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:46.930
Now the jury acquitted
Maxwell of an enticing charge,

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:49.020
but convicted her for transporting Jane

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.340
when she was a minor.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.220
And since Jane was then under 18,

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:54.510
the penalty is up to 15 years in jail.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.950
Now Maxwell was found
guilty of three charges

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.130
of conspiracy related to the charges

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.450
that we just talked about.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:03.220
Conspiracy to commit a sex
trafficking of a minor,

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.810
conspiracy to entice a
minor to travel to engage

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.100
in criminal sexual activity,

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:08.930
and conspiracy to transport a minor

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:12.150
with the intent to engage
in criminal sexual activity.

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.530
Prosecutors charged Maxwell
with conspiracy charges

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.380
for agreeing to do these crimes,

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.550
which was paired with
the substantive charges

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:20.790
for committing those specific crimes.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.620
Now to convict someone of conspiracy,

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.100
the prosecutor simply has to prove

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.270
that the defendant committed overt acts

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.480
in furtherance of the conspiracy.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.910
And remember, a conspiracy charge

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.030
is sort of an empty vessel.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:34.010
It requires a predicate illegal conduct

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:37.860
for which multiple people are
agreeing or helping out with.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:40.450
And here, the prosecution
laid out a criminal conspiracy

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.200
between Maxwell and Epstein
to abuse minor girls,

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.710
often by transporting them to
Epstein's house in New York,

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:47.280
Florida, New Mexico, and England.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.550
Maxwell encouraged underage
girls to participate

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.020
in these massages with Epstein
while they were in England,

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.630
all the while, knowing that the girls

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.090
would be sexually abused
during the massages.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.610
Maxwell was also charged
with enticing a female victim

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.000
to travel from Florida to New York

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.360
in order to facilitate
sex acts with Epstein.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.440
Now Maxwell's defense

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:05.270
was that she was just
an innocent bystander

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:08.250
who did not participate in
the abuse of the victims.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:09.660
Maxwell argued that the victims

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.500
had been manipulated by their lawyers.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:14.150
And she also argued that
Epstein manipulated Maxwell

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.930
using the same tactics
that he used on the girls.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:18.640
And the defense attorneys
challenged the memories

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:20.560
of the four victims who testified.

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:22.940
There were some discrepancies
in the victim's recollections

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:24.420
about what happened,
but generally speaking,

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:26.220
they'd seem to be pretty minor details.

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:28.360
And the jury clearly believed
that while the victims

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:31.180
might've gotten some of the
more minor details wrong

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.900
dealing with events that took place

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.380
almost 20 years ago,

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.600
that they believe the more important facts

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.430
that Epstein abused under-aged girls

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:40.540
and that Maxwell facilitated that abuse.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:42.710
That's not surprising given
the pilot logs establishing

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.470
that the girls traveled
with Epstein and Maxwell,

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.320
coupled with their testimony
about how Maxwell groomed them,

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:49.270
which damaged Maxwell's defense.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.790
And I guess the jury
didn't believe that Maxwell

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:53.167
was an innocent bystander.

00:11:53.167 --> 00:11:56.140
And the maximum penalty on
all five counts for Maxwell

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.150
is 65 years, but the guidelines

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:01.220
usually recommend lower sentences
for first time offenders.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.060
And the maximum penalty
rarely tells you anything

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:07.780
about the sentence that a
defendant will actually serve.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:09.770
Federal sentences are
almost always adjusted

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:11.940
depending on whether there
was aggravating factors

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.160
or mitigating factors.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.640
And these adjustments are found

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.800
in the federal sentencing guidelines.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.120
And it's likely Maxwell won't face

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.090
anything like 65 years in jail.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.190
Though she will definitely be
in jail for quite a long time.

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:24.860
Now when weighing Maxwell's sentence,

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.820
the judge will have to
consider the size and scope

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:29.090
of the criminal activity,
and the person's role in it.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:30.700
In the Maxwell's case,

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:34.620
Epstein's two pilots described
her as his number two.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.900
Epstein's former house
manager told the jury

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:40.370
that Maxwell described herself
as the lady of the house.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:42.550
Though if the judge finds
that she was a manager

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:45.130
or supervisor, but not
an organizer or leader,

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.700
then her exposure would
increase by only three levels.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.770
And if she was an
organizer, leader, manager,

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.490
or supervisor in any criminal activity,

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:54.190
her guideline score only
goes up by two levels.

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.760
Calculating actual sentences

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:58.400
can be a very fact intensive endeavor

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.670
and it can be kind of tricky.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.910
But federal prosecutors predict
that Maxwell's involvement

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:06.780
was significant enough to
warrant a 20 to 25-year sentence.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.390
Now, some people have
suggested that Maxwell

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.160
may look to cooperate with prosecutors

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.550
to reduce her sentence,

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:14.220
but since Epstein is dead
and prosecutors regard her

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:15.460
as his second in command,

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.470
it's not clear what
she really has to gain,

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:19.680
or what prosecutors would want with her.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:22.730
And that's not the end of
the road for Maxwell's woes.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:23.563
Later this year,

00:13:23.563 --> 00:13:24.680
she will stand trial on charges

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:26.400
that she lied under oath
about Epstein's abuse

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:27.600
of underage girls.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:29.250
And according to prosecutors, Maxwell,

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:31.670
perjured herself during a 2016 deposition

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:33.434
in the Virginia Giuffre case

00:13:33.434 --> 00:13:35.170
where she told lawyers under oath

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.440
that she did not know about
Epstein's abuse of the girls

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.900
and did not know about
recruitment and interactions

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.160
with underage girls.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:41.993
Though on the other hand,

00:13:41.993 --> 00:13:43.720
one of the quirks of conspiracy charges

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:46.350
is that the statute of
limitations doesn't run

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:48.510
until the last overt act in the conspiracy

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:49.343
has been committed.

00:13:49.343 --> 00:13:51.890
So even though we're talking
about events that took place

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:54.140
in the '90s and early 2000s,

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.930
the conspiracy still continued decades

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:59.410
after the initial predicate acts,

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:03.850
which means that the other
people who engaged in these acts

00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:07.810
and engaged in this conspiracy
can still be found guilty

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:09.300
of the conspiracy charges,

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:12.230
even though the underlying
statute of limitations

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:14.570
might have already run.

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:16.663
And it's clear that here
in the Maxwell trial,

00:14:16.663 --> 00:14:19.847
Maxwell was engaging in
all kinds of overt acts

00:14:19.847 --> 00:14:21.940
in furtherance of the conspiracy,

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:24.370
including trying to cover it up years

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:26.630
after the initial acts took place.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.630
So it's possible that other people

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:31.000
who might've engaged in
some of these actions

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.940
and engaged in these
overt acts and furtherance

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:36.790
of the conspiracy might
still be able to be brought

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:39.370
to justice, even though it were decades

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:40.550
after the initial acts.

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:42.280
But that's not the end of the story.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.100
Just one week after the guilty verdict,

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:45.960
two jurors spoke out to the media

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.470
about their own histories of sexual abuse.

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:50.630
Now, why would that be a problem?

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:53.230
Well, the jurors revealed that
they shared their experiences

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.000
of sexual abuse during jury deliberations.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:57.900
And one of the jurors, or both of them,

00:14:57.900 --> 00:14:59.750
may have failed to disclose their history

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.340
in a jury questionnaire.

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:04.730
Their revelations could result
in a new trial for Maxwell.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:06.070
The first juror, Scotty David,

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:08.583
identified only by his
first and middle names,

00:15:08.583 --> 00:15:11.520
told to reporters that he
talked about his experiences

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.830
as a victim to assuage
doubts that other jurors

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:16.110
had about the testimonies
of the alleged victims.

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:18.320
Quote, "I can't remember all the details.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:20.160
There are some things that run together.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.580
When I shared that, they were
able to sort of come around

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.890
on, they were able to come
around on the memory aspect

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:25.990
of the sexual abuse."

00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:27.800
He had allegedly answered no

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.860
to the question of whether
he'd ever been a victim

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.060
of such a crime.

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:33.280
And the second juror
told the "New York Times"

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.960
that they also shared
a personal experience

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.210
of sexual abuse that
appeared to help shape

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:38.730
the jury's discussions.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:39.740
Now, as you probably know,

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:41.210
during the jury selection process,

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.590
which is called voir dire,

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.810
lawyers have the
opportunity to screen jurors

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:46.650
for who will hear the case.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:49.150
Lawyers can strike a limited
number of potential jurors

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:52.150
for no cause whatsoever,
which means for any reason,

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:55.260
as long as the reason isn't
a person's race or gender.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.420
These are known as peremptory challenges.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:59.800
But lawyers or the
judge can also challenge

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:01.210
jurors for cause.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:03.420
Potential jurors are excused
for cause when the judge

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.720
finds that they cannot
decide the case impartially.

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:07.900
Now a person's experiences and opinions

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.370
don't automatically mean that
they are unable to perform

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:12.040
the duties of a juror.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.250
The same is true when someone

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.860
has a strong partisan opinion.

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:17.060
A gun reform advocate
would not automatically

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:19.500
be disqualified to sit
on the Rittenhouse jury,

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.470
nor would a gun rights advocate.

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:23.170
A person who has been sexually abused

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.310
is not necessarily
disqualified to sit on a jury

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.130
involving sexual assault.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.570
The key question is whether a person

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.590
can set aside their
opinions and experiences

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:33.050
to decide questions
fairly and impartially.

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:35.370
So how do judges and lawyers figure out

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:37.010
if someone can be impartial?

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.740
Well, during voir dire,
lawyers ask probing questions

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:43.010
to prospective jurors, and
the judge does as well.

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:45.770
Jurors are required to be
truthful in this process.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.700
And as long as the
prospective juror discloses

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:49.680
relevant facts, the judge
will usually take their word

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:51.210
for it if they say that they can set aside

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:53.810
their own feelings in order
to render a fair judgment.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.660
Now you may wonder whether
people have ever lied

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:56.493
to get on a jury.

00:16:56.493 --> 00:16:58.770
And although this has certainly happened,

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:00.410
it's also common for a juror,

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.640
upon examination by the judge,

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.730
to admit that they would
have trouble putting aside

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:06.400
their personal biases to
render a fair verdict,

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:09.180
which effectively excuses
themselves from the jury.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.330
And really, that's what lawyers

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:12.040
want conflicted jurors to do.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.170
They really don't want a
situation where a juror lies

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.380
about their ability to
render a fair verdict.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:18.260
So what's the standard for a fair trial

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.420
because a juror lied in
the voir dire process?

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:24.440
Well, the Supreme Court
outlined that standard in 1984.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.620
Quote, "We hold that to obtain a new trial

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:27.520
in such a situation,

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:29.480
a party must first demonstrate
that the juror failed

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:32.010
to answer honestly a material
question on voir dire.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.437
And then further show
that a correct response

00:17:34.437 --> 00:17:37.950
would have provided a valid
basis for a challenge for cause.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:40.310
The motives for concealing
information may vary,

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:42.930
but only those reasons that
affect a juror's impartiality

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.470
can truly be said to affect
the fairness of a trial."

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:47.380
So that is a two-pronged standard.

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:49.680
And regarding the first
prong, questions are material

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:51.610
if they have a natural
tendency to influence

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:54.470
or are capable of influencing
the judge's determination

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:56.340
whether a juror can be impartial.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:58.460
Circuit courts are split on
whether the Supreme Court's

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.260
first prong requires some level of intent

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:02.220
behind the juror's
misstatement or omission.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.370
The second circuit,
where Maxwell was tried,

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:05.610
requires showing that the juror

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:07.270
deliberately withheld information.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.830
Jurors cannot be faulted for failing

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:09.940
to disclose certain information

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.350
when they were never asked
during the course of voir dire

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:14.390
to make those kinds of disclosures.

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:15.706
With respect to the Maxwell case,

00:18:15.706 --> 00:18:17.850
David told "Reuters" that he flew

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:19.000
through the jury questionnaire,

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:20.340
and did not recall being asked

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:22.230
whether he had been a
victim of sexual abuse.

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.120
David told reporters he
would have answered honestly

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.220
if asked explicitly about that question.

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:27.410
Now regarding the second prong,

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:29.470
that requires the defendant
to show that if the juror

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:30.890
had told the truth,

00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:33.610
there would have been a valid
basis for a challenge strike.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:35.020
The second circuit cases hold

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:36.260
that the standard is satisfied

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.970
as long as the reasonable judge made aware

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:40.610
of the withheld information
would have excused the juror

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:43.780
for cause, even if the
disqualification was not mandatory.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:46.280
So in this case, would
Judge Nathan have concluded

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:48.370
under the totality of the circumstances

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:51.050
that the two jurors lacked
the capacity and the will

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:53.170
to decide the case based on the evidence?

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:54.440
Well, this is a high bar.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:55.790
Jury verdicts are usually overturned

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:59.380
only if there is an extreme
misconduct by that juror.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:01.880
For example, in the US versus Daugerdas,

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:04.930
five defendants were charged
with $7 billion in tax evasion.

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:06.910
Juror number one, Katherine Conrad,

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.250
wrote a letter after the verdict,

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.110
complimenting the
government on all their work

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:10.950
during the trial.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:12.860
And when the lawyers researched Conrad,

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:15.220
they discovered that she was
not the stay-at-home mother

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:16.740
with a bachelor's degree that she claimed

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:18.700
to be in the court forms.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:19.960
Conrad was actually a lawyer

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:22.250
who was suspended for chronic alcoholism.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.830
She had been convicted of several crimes,

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.450
including punching a police officer,

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:26.660
stealing a bag of shrimp.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:29.410
And there was a warrant out for
her arrest in another state.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:30.790
She lied about being a plaintiff

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.400
in an ongoing personal injury case.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.740
And she described her husband
as a reputed mob boss.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:38.230
Conrad was later arrested
after she defied a subpoena

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:40.630
to testify at the hearing
regarding a new trial.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.360
She admitted that she lied to make herself

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:44.170
more marketable as a juror.

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:47.660
And not surprisingly, the judge
vacated those convictions.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:48.670
Now in the Maxwell case,

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:50.220
the pre-trial questionnaire asked jurors

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:52.230
whether they had ever
been sexually abused.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.470
Those who answered yes
were later questioned

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:56.880
by Judge Nathan, the presiding judge,

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:58.430
about whether they could be impartial.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:00.890
And rule 33 of the Federal
Rules of Criminal Procedure

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:02.870
authorizes a district
court to grant a motion

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.590
for a new trial if the interest
